    <!-- https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Axis Mapping is related to an Appearance of an Entity Space
    and defines which Axis of the Entity Space (Source Axis) can be mapped to which Axis of the Reference Space
     (another Entity, Document or Asset Space). This relation can be further specified with an angle and accuracy.
     An AxisMapping object can only relate on Source Axis to one Reference Axis.
     Thus, typically, each Entity Space Appearance links to three Axis Mapping objects.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Axis Mapping</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A point that defines a boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Boundary Point</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Boundary Point Mapping describes the relation of an Entity Axis Boundary Point (Source Point)
        to the reference space. The relation can be expressed by Directional Properties of the RELOC Ontology
        (e.g., containedInFront/Right/Bottom etc.) and/or as a Normalized Coordinate in relation to the reference space.
        If both properties are given the the normalized coordinate is to be interpreted in the context of the area
        defined by the RELOC Property (e.g., Point &lt;reloc:containedInRight&gt; RefSpace.
        --&gt; &apos;0.5&apos; describes the center of the Right Area of the Reference Space)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Boundary Point Mapping</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


